<p>Iranian hermit Amou Haji ate carrion, drank from puddles, lived in a hole, smoked dung, and died at 94, a few months after bathing for the first time in 60 years. He said he became a hermit due to &#8220;emotional setbacks&#8221; after a heartbreak.</p>
<p>English merchant Nathaniel Bentley became known as Dirty Dick when he stopped washing in his late 30s. His filthy shop became a tourist attraction. Interestingly, he too was said to have changed after a ruined love affair, allegedly after his fiancée died on the eve of their wedding.  Charles Dickens knew of the story, which may have inspired that of Miss Havisham in <em>Great Expectations</em>.</p>
